    {"symbol": "🍴", "tooltip": "Duty and referent come apart at the fork — one codebase spawns thousands of acts, so the author cannot be the thing served."},
    {"symbol": "📜", "tooltip": "Provenance metadata on every generation is the pre-harm standard a court can actually inspect, unlike frozen weights."}
  ],
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "Where the duty attaches and what the personhood referent names are different problems.", "targets": ["AN-7", "AN-8"]},
    {"claim": "Training shapes the harm surface, but the duty-triggering act — this output, to this person, on this date — only crystallizes at inference.", "targets": ["AN-7"]},
    {"claim": "You cannot serve a frozen weight file for what a forked, prompt-wrapped instance did on a Tuesday.", "targets": ["AN-8"]},
    {"claim": "Make adequate capitalization a condition of duty-bearing status, tied to upstream liability, set high enough that draining it triggers the developer's own duty.", "targets": []},
    {"claim": "Attach duty to the codebase and you have killed every open release, concentrated the field into three labs that can self-insure, and built the exact crumple zone you accused me of.", "targets": ["AN-5"]}
  ]
