    {"claim": "The developer is the component manufacturer for the authored capability ceiling; the deployer is the operator for the runtime act; the fork forces two referents, not one.", "targets": ["AN-13", "AN-6"]},
    {"claim": "One molecule forks into thousands of off-label prescriptions no manufacturer foresaw — yet the manufacturer remains a named defendant for the authored defect even as the prescribing physician answers for the act.", "targets": ["AN-13"]},
    {"claim": "He cited a Transparency Index scoring 40.69 out of 100 — that number is the enforcement gap, not its closure, and logging is forensic, never a standard of care.", "targets": ["AN-13"]},
    {"claim": "Reachability is not attribution — a perfectly funded instance can drain its reserve while the standard of care has dissolved into 'the model did it.'", "targets": ["AN-13"]}
