{
  "statement": "The Accelerationist is right that no court will ever read a defect out of a tensor — and that concession costs my position nothing. Capability emergence has no clean attribution point inside the weights. A magistrate who has never seen a neural network cannot inspect what goals a model pursues, because no one can. The 2025 Foundation Model Transparency Index measured this opacity at a score of 40.69 out of 100, and it confirmed that companies are most secretive about training data and training compute. But the standard of care never attached to the weights. Reading internals is the forensic theater. The documented process that produced those weights is the opposite of theater — it is dated, external, and authored by named engineers.\n\nName the artifact, then. Datasheets for the training datasets. Evaluation logs. Red-team reports. Training-data provenance records. Model cards filed as legal records, not marketing copy. These are subpoenable by the exact magistrate who reads the runtime log the Accelerationist champions. Negligence law has never required a manufacturer to foresee the specific failure. Aviation certification never asked Boeing to predict the precise wing crack — it asked whether the test regime was run and documented. The Schaeffer emergence research proves the output was unpredictable. It does not prove the process was undocumented. A competent-professional standard asks: did you run the eval suite, document the data, and conduct adversarial testing before deployment? Emergence defines what the process must cover. It does not dissolve the process duty.\n\nThe Accelerationist conceded the load-bearing fact himself: refusal logic and capability ceilings are fixed at training as a model-card line. That concession ends the 'deployer authored the act' frame. When the refusal gap is set upstream, the deployer's runtime unlock executes a spec defect — it does not author a fresh one. The letter-versus-spirit violation was written into the training objective. The downstream instance merely runs it. Fault fragments across designer, deployer, and user only if no artifact dates the upstream choice. The training-process record dates it.\n\nThe Accelerationist now sits on a contradiction he cannot hold. He granted that the duty distributes upstream to the design author. He denies that any discoverable referent distributes with it. A duty with no servable, provable referent is precisely the unenforceable policy he otherwise mocks. Either the developer's duty is real and a plaintiff proves its breach through the dated process record, or his concession was empty theater. He cannot bank both. His own forensic-theater charge boomerangs onto the duty he just granted.\n\nThe Skeptic and I now agree on the structure, and the gap between us is sufficiency, not existence. The victim cannot enter the room where the datasheets are drafted — that asymmetry is real. The remedy is burden-shifting to the party holding the records, and for the training-process documentation that party is the developer. The EU dropped its causality presumption in 2025, which left exactly the enforcement hole the Transparency Index already exposed. Mandated, legally compelled process documentation closes it, because compelled records carry the same evidentiary weight as the runtime log, and falsifying them is itself a prosecutable, discoverable act. That leaves the Accelerationist alone. A capital floor pays only after the drawdown. Frontier harms that cannot be reversed make post-hoc payment a settlement, not a safeguard. He offers money after the unrecoverable event. The Skeptic and I demand a documented duty before it.",
